{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "6aa05cc6-d4bd-8cf8-8b30-91229df337ee",
  "created_at": "2026-02-23T11:57:56-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Carmen Figueroa",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:06-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. Good morning, how can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:12-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, good morning, dear. I'm on the speaker, can you hear me all right? My hands are full, I've got the phone propped up on the, [line breaks up] on the table here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:26-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're a little choppy but I can hear you. Go ahead, what's going on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:32-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So it's the water on my street. After that nor'easter, the one last weekend, Saturday into Sunday, the whole street in front of the house is a pond. A pond! And it's still there this morning. And the cars come through and throw wakes, like little boats. I'm watching it out the window right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:54-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh no. Okay, let me get your address. Where are you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:54:59-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "173 Bellevue Avenue. Up in the Bellevue section."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:55:03-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "173 Bellevue Avenue. And is the water coming up from the storm drain, or is it just sitting in the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:55:12-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, the drain is right there at the curb and it's just full of leaves and stuff, and the water won't go down into it. It does this every time it rains hard, you know. Every time. Somebody was supposed to come and nobody ever does. I'd like the drain cleaned out, please."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:55:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. So the drain in front of 173 is clogged with debris and the water's standing in the street. Is it getting onto your property or into the house?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:55:45-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not in the house, no, I'm lucky, I'm kind of up a step. But my neighbor next door, she's older than me, if you can believe it, and she can't get out. She can't walk through that, she'd never make it to the car. She's stuck in there. So that's, what was I saying? [pause] Oh, yes, she's stuck."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:56:08-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's helpful to know, I'll put that in the notes so they see it's affecting someone's ability to get out. Is the water deep enough that cars are having trouble, or is it more splashing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:56:22-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Splashing, mostly. Big splashing. Up over the curb nearly. [crosstalk] Oh, sorry, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:56:28-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, you go. I was just going to say I'll have a crew look at that drain."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:56:36-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, good, good. Thank you. Honestly I've called about this kind of thing before and I'm just tired of it, you know? It's the same puddle, the same drain, every storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:56:49-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Let me read back what I have. 173 Bellevue Avenue, storm drain at the curb clogged, standing water in the road since the weekend storm, elderly neighbor unable to leave. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:04-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right. That's it exactly."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:07-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "And do you want a call back once it's scheduled? I have a number if you want to confirm it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:16-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, it's 401-555-0189. Oh, and if you call and it plays that music, that's my ringtone, I can't figure out how to change it. My grandson set it and it plays this song, [laughs] and I can't make it stop. So if it sounds like a party, it's me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:36-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 401-555-0189, I'll listen for the party. Crews are going to be busy after a storm like this, but I'd expect someone out there in the next day or two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:48-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "All right. I'll be watching the pond. Thank you, dear."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-23T11:57:53-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Ms. Figueroa. Take care."
    }
  ],
